A circular queue is a linear data structure that overcomes the limitations of a simple queue. In a normal array implementation, dequeue() can be O(n) or we may waste space. Using a circular array, both enqueue() and dequeue() can be done in O(1).Declaration using Array:In this implementation, arr is used to store elements. some variables are maintained:arr[] : array to store elements.capacity : maximum size of the queue.front : index of the front element.size : current number of elements in the queue.
